# Breachboard

Gamified cyber tabletop exercise (TTX) app for live facilitated runs: scenarios, injects, roles, scoring, and org onboarding.

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router (`app/`), React 19, TypeScript
- Prisma + PostgreSQL (host port **5433** in dev)
- NextAuth credentials (`lib/auth.ts`, `OPERATOR_EMAIL` / `OPERATOR_PASSWORD`)
- AI scenario generation via Vercel AI SDK (`lib/ai/`, providers in `lib/ai/providers.ts`)
- Tailwind v4 + custom design tokens (`design/tokens.css`, `app/globals.css`)

## Run

```bash
./run.sh          # local dev → http://localhost:3000
./run.sh docker   # full stack → http://localhost:3080
```

Env: `.env.local` (dev) or `.env` (docker). Copy from `.env.example`.

## Key paths

| Area | Location |
|------|----------|
| Live session UI | `components/session-console.tsx`, `components/game-ui.tsx` |
| Scenario schema | `lib/schema/exercise.ts` |
| Session API | `app/api/sessions/[id]/route.ts` |
| Generate flow | `app/generate/page.tsx`, `lib/ai/generate-scenario.ts` |
| Access control | `lib/access.ts` — admin vs participant |
| Score helpers | `lib/game-score.ts` |

## Domain model

- **Exercise** — scenario document (JSON): roles, injects, questions, points, ATT&CK map
- **ExerciseSession** — one live run with join code, status (`draft` / `live` / `closed`), current inject
- **SessionSeat** — user seated as MODERATOR, OBSERVER, or PARTICIPANT (+ playbook role)
- **InjectAnswer** — participant response per inject (unique per user per inject)

## UI conventions

Follow `.cursor/rules/design.mdc`: Pitch Obsidian default, toxic phosphor accent, optional elite liquid glass finish. Mono for join codes, ATT&CK IDs, hashes, and terminal prompts. Gamified copy for participant surfaces; admin surfaces use command/ops language.

## When changing

- Schema changes: update `prisma/schema.prisma`, run `npx prisma migrate dev` (production: `migrate deploy`). See `docs/DEPLOY.md`.
- New LLM provider: extend `llmProviderSchema` in `lib/schema/exercise.ts` and `lib/ai/providers.ts`
- Do not commit `.env` / `.env.local` with real secrets
